# The build context is what `cargo build --release` reads: the two workspaces,
# their manifests and lockfiles, the source trees, and the default config.
# Everything excluded here is either a host build artifact (large, and built for
# the wrong architecture) or something only tests, docs and CI consume — the
# image never runs tests, and `Cargo.toml` dev-dependencies do not need the test
# files to exist for `cargo build` to succeed.
.git/
.github/
.superpowers/
.worktrees/
target/
xdp/target/
docs/
scripts/
tests/
crates/*/tests/
*.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
.gitignore
*.log
